00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.800
Become a Title22 partner: what a code does, what it pays, and where referrals come from.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:18.000
Three ways in. You teach the courses. You work around care homes but don't teach. Or you took the course and now run a home — being a customer doesn't stop you being a partner.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:27.000
A code is a longer trial. Someone who signs up through your link gets 90 days free, instead of the standard 30.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.500
You get one row per code: your link, how many signed up, how many are paying, and your rate. Attribution happens when the account is created.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:47.500
You earn on paid subscriptions, not signups — every month they stay. 20% is the default. Your rate is agreed with Eli, and he pays you directly.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:58.500
Two things to know. Only signups are tracked, not clicks. And a code can't attach to an account that already exists — so send your link before they sign up.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:09.500
The referrals that convert: your own graduates the week they're licensed, homes fresh from an inspection, and anyone hiring or opening a second home.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:18.700
The line that works is simple: "Use my link, and you get 90 days free instead of 30." It is specific, true, and free to check.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:29.700
To start, email hello@title-22.com and confirm your rate. You'll get a link you can reuse forever. If you teach, ask for a classroom account too.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:38.300
Everything is at title-22.com/partners. Email hello@title-22.com to get your code.
